Z||000000||Brian84SE||09-19-2000||08:26 PM||||I took the throttle body of my iron puke and looking into the intake I noticed a small piece of sheet metal on an angle in the bore.  What is it  for?  Smooth out the fuel/air mix?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-19-2000||11:09 PM||||It suposedly helps balance flow in the intake. Leave it there. GM wouldn't have spent money on it if it wasn't some kind of issue they thought important.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||09-20-2000||01:17 PM||||The "restrictor plate" helps ballance the fuel/air mixture to the center 2 cyl and outer 2 cyls. Without it cylendar 2 and 3 would get more gas/air than cyl 1 and $ causing the car to hesatate when accelerating. The two center cyl would run rich and 1 & 4 lean. no ballance of power/ingnition of gas/air. Leave it in. (boy oh boy mu computer is haveing a bad spelling day LOL) <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||4
